Exercise: sa-lvm-review (chapter 18 lab)

Work on serverb, with sudo or as root, on the spare disk /dev/sdb (5 GiB,
empty). Do not touch /dev/sda.

Physical and logical layers
 1. Two LVM partitions of 1.5 GiB each on /dev/sdb (GPT, flag lvm).
 2. A volume group vgapp with an extent size of 8 MiB (vgcreate -s 8M),
    created on the first partition only.
 3. Logical volumes in vgapp:
      - lvweb, 1 GiB, XFS, mounted on /srv/web
      - lvdb, 400 MiB, ext4, mounted on /srv/db
      - lvswap, 256 MiB, used as swap
    The group is too small for all three: when lvcreate complains, add
    the second partition to vgapp.
 4. Put a file /srv/web/numbers.txt in lvweb that contains the numbers 1 to
    100000 (seq 1 100000), then grow lvweb to at least 2000 MiB, with its
    file system, while it is mounted. The file must still be there.

Permanent
 5. Entries in /etc/fstab for the two file systems and the swap volume.
    Test with findmnt --verify, mount -a and swapon -a.

On workstation
 6. Fill in answers.txt.

Then, on workstation:  lab grade sa-lvm-review
